-- title:
--   Primitives of regular differentials along paths exist, unique up to constants
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a field equipped with a $\mathbb{C}$-algebra structure, assumed to contain an element $x$ transcendental over $\mathbb{C}$ such that $F$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $\mathbb{C}(x)$ generated by $x$, and assumed to satisfy `IsCurveOver ℂ F`: every nonzero $f \in F$ has a degree-zero divisor whose value at each place $v$ is $\mathrm{ord}_v(f) = -\log v(f)$, every residue field of a place is finite over $\mathbb{C}$, and $\Omega[F/\mathbb{C}]$ is free of rank one over $F$. The set `Place ℂ F` of places carries a Hausdorff topology and a $\mathbb{C}$-charted structure making it an analytic ($\omega$-smooth) manifold, and it is assumed that for every $f \neq 0$ and every place $v$ the function $z \mapsto \mathrm{evalAt}_{\varphi_v^{-1}(z)}(f)$, where $\varphi_v$ is the extended chart at $v$, is meromorphic at $\varphi_v(v)$ with meromorphic order there equal to $\mathrm{ord}_v(f)$. Let $\eta \in \Omega[F/\mathbb{C}]$ be regular, i.e. for each place $v$ one has $\eta = f \cdot v.\mathrm{dCoord}$ for some $f$ in the valuation subring of $v$, where $v.\mathrm{dCoord} = D_{\mathbb{C}/F}(\pi_v)$ for the uniformiser $\pi_v$, and let $\gamma$ be a path from a place $P$ to a place $Q$. Then, first, there is $g : [0,1] \to \mathbb{C}$ that is a primitive of $\eta$ along $\gamma$, meaning that for each $t_0$ there is $\Phi : \mathbb{C} \to \mathbb{C}$ having, at all $z$ in a neighbourhood of $\varphi_{\gamma(t_0)}(\gamma(t_0))$, derivative equal to the chart reading $(\gamma t_0).\mathrm{readDifferential}\ \eta$ of $\eta$ at that point (the product of the chart read of the coefficient of $\eta$ with the derivative of the chart read of `dCoordFn`), and such that $g(t) = \Phi(\varphi_{\gamma(t_0)}(\gamma(t)))$ for all $t$ near $t_0$; and second, any two such primitives $g, g'$ satisfy $g(t) - g'(t) = g(0) - g'(0)$ for all $t$.
--
--   This is the existence and essential uniqueness of local primitives of a holomorphic differential along a path on the Riemann surface of places of a complex function field in one variable, the analytic input behind path integration of regular differentials. It makes the path integral of $\eta$ along $\gamma$ well defined independently of the chosen primitive, and is used in the construction of the Abel–Jacobi map and its period lattice (for instance in [`AlgebraicCurve.exists_abelJacobiDiv_sub_mem_pathPeriodLattice_and_image_mem_nhds`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.exists_abelJacobiDiv_sub_mem_pathPeriodLattice_and_image_mem_nhds)).
